devex-mia: Heads-up: saw a weird flake in samplekit when using JSON mode + streaming + fncall. model streams JSON chunks, retry wrapper resends and we end up with doubled partial fragments that the helper glues incorrectly.
sdk-ryan: Oof. streaming + retries is always tricky. Can you paste the stream fragments?
devex-mia: minimal trace from local run:\n```\nSTREAM CHUNK 1:\n{"id": "tool-run", "result": {"items": ["a"\nSTREAM CHUNK 2 (retry fired):\n{"id": "tool-run", "result": {"items": ["b"]}}\n```\nThe python helper's recombine step saw two objects and merged arrays into ["a","b"], but the TS helper's stream parser preferred the last complete object and returned only {items:["b"]}. downstream validator expected single object with items list in order and tests failed.
eng-oncall-zoe: why did retry fire mid-stream? the retry policy should only kick on non-2xx or parse errors, not partial streaming.
devex-mia: seems our safe-retry timeout triggers if no activity for 250ms, and the model's next chunk arrived at 300ms due to network jitter. policy assumed stateless idempotent requests; not safe for streaming chunked fncalls.
ml-alex: also worth noting that some models send incremental partial JSON like "items": ["a", and then continue. recombiner must treat stream boundaries carefully.
sdk-ryan: proposed fixes: 1) make retry-for-streams conservative (only retry on connection drop or explicit error) 2) add deterministic stream-recombine semantics in both SDKs: always concat partials and attempt full-JSON reconciliation, preserving order. 3) add an opt-in "stream_atomic_fncall" flag to force single-shot behavior.
sam-dev: for onboarding samplekit, i think we should turn off aggressive retry and document this caveat prominently. demos should use stream_atomic_fncall:true for now.
eng-oncall-zoe: agree. i'll change the default retry threshold for streaming endpoints to 1s and only retry on network-level errors.
sdk-ryan: i'll add a shared test that simulates interleaved chunks + retry and assert both py/ts helpers return identical normalized output. also adding e2e test in samplekit.
devex-mia: can we add a small heuristics note in the SDK docs about partial-json streaming? maybe a snippet showing safe recombine logic.
ml-alex: snippet i usually share:```js
// naive recombine: buffer fragments until parseable
let buf = "";
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  buf += chunk;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = ""; // reset for next object
  } catch (e) {
    // not enough data yet, continue
  }
}
```
But emphasize ordering and idempotency concerns.
sam-dev: PR incoming to samplekit to set stream_atomic_fncall default true for quickstarts + update docs.
deploy-bot: deploy-bot: samplekit quickstart config will flip stream_atomic_fncall=true in v1.8.4 on merge. :package:
devex-mia: action list: (1) zoe adjust retry policy for streams (2) ryan add parity stream recombine tests (3) sam merge samplekit PR and docs update (4) alex author example heuristics note. i'll monitor support for any tickets referencing streaming fncall flake.
sdk-ryan: i'll also add a telemetry tag for "stream_retries" so we can see frequency.
eng-oncall-zoe: started a hotfix branch, ETA 4h.
devex-mia: thanks everyone. even though it's niche, streaming fncall combos are important for low-latency apps. saved a demo today! :raised_hands:
